# Copy to .env (already git-ignored) and fill in. Never commit .env.
# The stock research digest (npm run research) reads these.

# Alpaca: market data only. Create a free account, open the Paper
# trading dashboard, and generate API keys there. Phase 1 uses them
# only for prices and news on data.alpaca.markets; no orders.
ALPACA_API_KEY_ID=your-alpaca-key-id
ALPACA_API_SECRET_KEY=your-alpaca-secret-key

# Anthropic API key from console.anthropic.com. Set a monthly spend
# limit in the console too, as a second cap behind the daily one below.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your-anthropic-api-key

# The SEC asks every client to identify itself with a name and contact
# email. Free, no key.
SEC_USER_AGENT="Stocky research your-email@example.com"

# Optional settings (defaults shown).
# Comma-separated tickers. Default is 20 large US stocks; see src/research/config.ts.
# STOCKY_WATCHLIST=AAPL,MSFT,NVDA
# How many names get a Claude write-up each day.
# RESEARCH_PER_DAY=8
# Hard daily cap on Claude spend in US dollars.
# RESEARCH_DAILY_BUDGET_USD=0.75
# RESEARCH_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
# Budget routing: when set, only the first RESEARCH_PREMIUM_PER_DAY
# picks (fresh filings first, then highest interest) use RESEARCH_MODEL
# and the rest use this cheaper model, so the same budget covers more
# names. Unset means every pick uses RESEARCH_MODEL.
# RESEARCH_BUDGET_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5
# RESEARCH_PREMIUM_PER_DAY=3
# Discovery: before the daily pick, scan about 100 more large US stocks
# and add the few with unusual moves, volume, news or 8-K filings. They
# share the daily limit and budget above. on or off.
# RESEARCH_DISCOVERY=on
# How many new finds can join a day's list.
# RESEARCH_DISCOVERY_ADD=3
# How unusual a name must look to qualify (same scale as the watchlist).
# RESEARCH_DISCOVERY_MIN_INTEREST=2
# Which built-in list discovery scans: large (about 100 big names, the
# default), small (about 200 smaller, lesser-known US stocks with a
# looser liquidity floor), or both. Free IEX data runs thinner on small
# caps, so expect more noise and sparser news there.
# RESEARCH_UNIVERSE=large
# Comma-separated tickers to scan instead of the built-in lists.
# STOCKY_DISCOVERY_UNIVERSE=ORCL,CRM,ADBE
# Dead-man alert for the scheduled research run, like the collector's
# STOCKY_HEARTBEAT_URL: a healthchecks.io check URL pinged on success,
# with /fail appended on failure. Give the check a weekday 12:30 UTC
# schedule so a run that never starts also alerts. Unset means off.
# Dry runs and --as-of replays never ping it.
# RESEARCH_HEARTBEAT_URL=https://hc-ping.com/your-check-uuid
# Phone push when the scheduled run finishes, through ntfy (ntfy.sh or
# self-hosted): the full topic URL to POST to. Pick a long random topic
# name; anyone who knows it can read the pushes. Unset means off.
# RESEARCH_NTFY_URL=https://ntfy.sh/your-long-random-topic
# Where tapping the push opens, for example the research page on your
# tailnet. Optional.
# RESEARCH_PAGE_URL=https://your-pi.your-tailnet.ts.net/research.html
